messages:
Priya: Quick sync — Nebula onboarding. Mobile SDK (iOS/Android 1.4.0) is seeing 401s followed by a burst of 429s when the app resumes and our serverless endpoints warm up. Repro on their device (Android 12). Anyone seen background refresh + warmup races like this?
Alex: Can you paste the logs and confirm which auth flow they're using (ephemeral v1/v2 or long-lived)?
Priya: Ephemeral v2 tokens. Sample logs below (redacted):
```
[auth] 2026-03-20T16:12:03Z GET /token 200 ttl=30s
[app] 2026-03-20T16:12:04Z background_refresh start (resume)
[auth] 2026-03-20T16:12:04Z POST /auth/refresh 500 internal
[app] 2026-03-20T16:12:04Z retry -> 200 token ttl=30s
[proxy] 2026-03-20T16:12:06Z request surge -> 429 rate_limit
```
Marco: TTL=30s is pretty tight. Looks like many clients refresh around the same time (resume) and warmups amplify the fanout. Two short-term fixes: 1) increase ephemeral TTL for onboarding customers (eg. 180–300s) and 2) add jitter + exponential retry in the SDK refresh path.
Alex: Agreed. We can bump TTL for Nebula from the console as a stop-gap. Marco — can you post the suggested SDK change we can share with them and ship in patch?
Marco: Suggested patch (pseudo):
```js
// previous: refresh exactly at fixed window
const REFRESH_WINDOW = 30; // sec
setTimeout(refreshToken, REFRESH_WINDOW);

// new: proportional window + jitter + backoff
const refreshWindow = Math.max(10, Math.floor(token.ttl * 0.25));
const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.floor(refreshWindow * 0.5));
setTimeout(() => refreshToken(), refreshWindow + jitter);

// on 5xx/429 -> exponential backoff with capped retries
function refreshToken() {
  // attempt + on failure schedule retry with backoff
}
```
Priya: @Sam can you coordinate with Nebula to test after we bump TTL? I'll create a short verification window. Also capturing this as a renewal risk if spikes keep happening.
Sam: On it — I'll ping them now and request they test between 17:00-17:15 PT. If they confirm lower error rate after TTL bump + SDK patch, we'll mark as mitigated.
cs-bot: Deploy 2850 to token-service succeeded (2026-03-20T17:08:00Z) :white_check_mark:
Alex: Follow-ups: instrument a metric token_refresh_concurrency{account} and alert if >100 concurrent refreshes/min for an account. Also add a dashboard so CS can see refresh storms.
Priya: Perfect. I'll update the onboarding ticket with the TTL bump and SDK recommendation, and follow up with Nebula after Sam's check-in. Thanks everyone :pray:
